# Kami CLA

- Community Edition stays MIT. The CLA is a **license grant** (not assignment) so maintainers can later dual-license / ship Enterprise without re-collecting grants.
- Every human PR author and committer must sign by commenting: `I have read the CLA Document and I hereby sign the CLA`
- Do not allowlist `@saranambiar` or `@VaradDurge`. They sign once; the bot stores it on `cla-signatures`.
- Allowlist only bots (`bot*`, `cursor[bot]`, `cursoragent`, Dependabot, github-actions).
- Never hand-edit `signatures/version1/cla.json`. Comment `recheck` on the PR if status is stale.
- Signatures live on the unprotected `cla-signatures` branch. Do not point the workflow `branch:` at `main` or `dev`.
- Do not weaken CLA checks to land a PR. Do not replace the CLA with DCO unless both maintainers agree.
- Legal/automation file owners: both maintainers (see CODEOWNERS).
